    {
      "id": "3d-printed-portable-pc",
      "title": "3D Printed Portable PC",
      "summary": "A refined take on the 3D Printed Portable PC.",
      "tags": [
        "Computer"
      ],
      "versions": [
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "This is a new case design for a powerful, compact rig that has a small removable tray on the right for cables, dongles, controllers, etc.",
          "source": "V1_Assembly.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-assembly/v1.step"
        },
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added holes for USB ports, power button and ventilation for the GPU",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v1.step"
        },
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added ventilation for the CPU cooler",
          "source": "V1_Cover.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-cover/v1.step"
        },
        {
          "id": "v2",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added magnet holes for the cover and chamfers to ensure it will work on an FDM printer",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v2.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v3",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Moved the back wall 3mm due to interference with the motherboard IO shield",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v3.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v4",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Increased the thickness of the PCIE holder since it was too thin to be printed",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v4.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v5",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added a chamfer to the PCIE finger for DFAM",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v5.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v6",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Moved the GPU power connector cutout to relieve potential strain on cable",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v6.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v2",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added holes for magnets to secure the cover to the Case_Base",
          "source": "V1_Cover.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-cover/v2.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Cover": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Model for the top fan filters. A cutout is made for the handle. Magnet holes as well. A small, 1mm wide, 0.6mm cutout is placed around the border to improve the visual seam",
          "source": "V1_Fan_Filter.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-fan-filter/v1.step"
        },
        {
          "id": "v7",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added magnet holes for the top fan filter. Also added 13x13mm magnet cutouts for the removable side cover. Added 45 degree pegs to secure the bottom half of said side cover",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v7.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v8",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Added a 1mm wide, 0.6mm deep cutout to improve the seams of the design.",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v8.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v2",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Iterating from my previous designs, this version goes back to Air cooling and is focused more on ease of use and consistency. The IO is in a more traditional orientation as opposed to the vertical layout of before. It also adds front USB ports to make it easier to add/remove peripherals. A removable right section is added to store cables/peripherals during transport.",
          "source": "V1_Assembly.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-assembly/v2.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Assembly_inchObj": "added",
            "V1_Assembly_mmObj": "added",
            "V1_Assembly": "modified"
          },
          "removed": [
            "USB Female_1",
            "USB-C Frontplug AliExpress_1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "v3",
          "date": "2026-11-15",
          "note": "Learning from previous iterations, this portable PC goes back to air cooling and has a more traditional layout to make it easier for the end user to install/uninstall peripherals. It also adds front IO for easier peripheral insertion and a removable section that can store cables/peripherals during travel.",
          "source": "V1_Assembly.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-assembly/v3.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Assembly": "modified"
          },
          "removed": [
            "V1_Assembly_inchObj",
            "V1_Assembly_mmObj"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "date": "2026-11-16",
          "note": "This is the preliminary design for the removable box on the PC case. Unfortunately due to the dimensions, a standard Xbox controller is too large to fit inside, but I can make a spot for cables and a mouse.",
          "source": "V1_Snap_Box.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-snap-box/v1.step"
        },
        {
          "id": "v9",
          "date": "2026-11-16",
          "note": "Added dovetails and split the body into four sections for printing. Also moved the back magnet clip back 3mm to align with the IO being pushed back in an earlier revision.",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v9.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v10",
          "date": "2026-11-16",
          "note": "Added dovetails to the PSU side of the base to increase rigidity",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v10.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v11",
          "date": "2026-11-16",
          "note": "Thickened the PCIE bar and moved the IO cutout for improved access to ports. Small chamfers to increase stiffness.",
          "source": "V1_Case_Base.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-case-base/v11.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Case_Base": "modified"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "v3",
          "date": "2026-11-16",
          "note": "Added vent holes to the back of the cover. Intentionally made it so there are more vent holes going in than out so that the case has \"positive\" pressure and will help prevent dust from getting inside of it.",
          "source": "V1_Cover.stp",
          "file": "projects/3d-printed-portable-pc/v1-cover/v3.step",
          "changes": {
            "V1_Cover": "modified"
          }
        }
      ],
